services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 5. Contract [1], for 14,228 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December and the high number of unique awardees do not prove improper conduct. Statistical patterns can arise from market conditions or budget constraints, not wrongdoing. The data reflects trends, not violations.\nWhat can be checked: Check the contracts awarded in December for consistency with other contracts. Verify if awardee A has repeated orders for the same service. Review if multiple contracts cover the same need to ensure no overlap or duplication.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["TyAAKWOsum0mMOlAXxDEjw%3D%3D","HxL6uuz5q5L%2Fa9DgO%2BoYKQ%3D%3D","qaY9UVb3a3ZVq4S9zvaQpQ%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}